  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 326 PM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nUpper pattern features a Pacific jet nosing into the Northern\nPlains out of the Canadian Rockies. At the surface, a weak and\ndry front is moving through the region this afternoon into\nevening. This may allow for some sprinkles, but overall lack of\nmoisture and temperature change behind the front will prevent\nmost rain from reaching the ground.\n\nPost frontal air mass tomorrow will be noticed mostly by an\nincrease in northwest winds, gusting 25-35 mph, perhaps nearing\n40 mph in northwest MN during the afternoon. Also in northwest\nMN, some rain showers may develop lee of Lake of the Woods \nduring the afternoon. Lower RH values in southeast ND will allow\nfor near critical fire weather conditions, however relatively\nhigher moisture fuel status will negate any dedicated messaging\nof fire weather concerns at this time.\n\nInto late week, upper pattern stays rather zonal with some\nguidance suggesting upper ridging into the central CONUS by next\nweek. This will continue to support above average temperatures\nand an overall dry forecast.",
